Honestly, most of these would do nothing to me. I'm not picking a snack based on what it says on the wrapper. It's whatever's reduced and whatever's in the vending machine at the depot, which I'm not even at now. A bit of text on a Dairy Milk saying it'll give me bowel cancer, I'd read it, go "right" and buy it anyway. The posters have been telling me for years and I've never once clocked them.

The calorie badge is the one that might actually make me think for a second. I don't count anything, but if I can see a fruit pot's a fraction of a Galaxy I might grab that. Though a tenner's still a tenner, so it's more about what I can afford than what's good for me. The gory photos would stick in my head a bit more, I'll admit, but I'd probably just look away and grab the Doritos. And if it's all in the frame of "make every mouthful count," I'm switching off before I've finished reading it.

