Honestly, most of these would wash over me. I'm not going to change what I buy because a packet has a scary picture on it. I know Dairy Milk isn't health food. What decides it is whether I'm knackered after a late shift and whether it's cheap and filling enough to get me through.

The calorie badges are the only ones with a bit of real info, because I do check the spreadsheet and I'd notice if a fruit pot was 95 and a bar was 240. Even so, I'd still grab whatever's in the chiller reduced to 20p if it means I'm not eating a bag of apple crisps at half eleven and still hungry. The graphic medical photos would probably just annoy me. The plain text warnings I'd barely register. And if nothing's changed on the packets, I'd buy exactly what I was going to buy anyway.

