Honestly, most of these would wash over me. The guilt-trip ones especially. Bowel tumour on a packet of Doritos? I'd think "right, thanks" and grab them anyway, same as I do with the cigarette warnings. The plain text one is only marginally better.

The calorie badges are the only thing that might actually register. I already check the price per kilo on the shelf label before buying pasta, so a big bold number is the same sort of thing. Seeing 95 next to 240 might make me reach for the apple crisps once in a while, though I'm not promising anything. I'd still probably buy the Dairy Milk on a bad day. Showing me the snacks with no labels is basically how it is now, so that changes nothing.

