Honestly, most of these would wash over me. The five-a-day posters already don't work on me, and I suspect the graphic ones would just make me roll my eyes. A bowel tumour on a Dairy Milk wrapper? I'd think "fair enough" and buy the Dairy Milk anyway, probably with a bit of spite.

The calorie badges are the only ones that might actually change something. I run, so I'd notice a number like "240" and maybe think twice about a second biscuit, even if I'd still pick the Galaxy on a bad day. The plain text warnings feel preachy, which is the thing that puts me off. Doing nothing at all is basically what happens now.

