Honestly, most of these would wash over me. I've seen plenty of warnings on packets and I just stop reading them. The black-and-white text ones blur into the rest of the packaging, and the graphic photos would probably make me look away and grab whatever's cheapest. Fear doesn't pay the bills, and it doesn't change what's in my bag at the Co-op on the way home.

A bold calorie number is the only thing that might catch my eye for two seconds. If a fruit pot says 95 and a Galaxy says 250, I'd notice that, even if I'd still probably pick the Galaxy on a Friday. The shelf price matters more to me than any label, so nothing here touches the budget problem.

