Right, my first thought is that the pictures would just put me off the whole lot, and I'd still be standing there with the same four quid. A bowel tumour on a packet of Doritos is a bit much. My sister would forward it with "SEE, THIS IS WHY" and I'd have to ignore her again.

The calorie badge is the one that might actually do something. I already work out price per kilo, so seeing "240 CALORIES" next to a Dairy Milk and "95" on a fruit pot would make the choice quick. It doesn't make the fruit pot cheaper, mind. Plain text warnings are just noise to me. I've read a hundred of those on packets and they've never changed a thing. Shelves with no labels at all are how they already are, so nothing changes there either.

