Honestly, most of these would wash over me. The shock pictures would put me off, not the crisps. I'd feel lectured, and I'd just stop looking at the packet. A number on the front is different. A "240 CALORIES" badge I can actually use. I'd glance at it next to the fruit pot and think, right, that's the one. It's not much, but it's something I can weigh up quickly, unlike a scare photo or a finger-wagging line.

The plain text warnings are just more of the "we're all children" tone, so I'd skip past them. And the snacks as they already are tell me nothing new, which is how it's always been.

