Honestly, the warnings would just wash over me. I've read the packet before, and "excess calories cause obesity" is hardly news. The graphic photos would probably make me roll my eyes, as if they think I need frightening into eating a carrot. Plain text on a crisp packet, I'd not even notice.

The calorie numbers are the only bit that might do something. I cut back on crisps and biscuits because my trousers got tight, so seeing "240 CALORIES" next to a Dairy Milk might make me think twice, especially if a fruit pot is sat right next to it at 95. I'm not one for rules, but a number I can compare is different. I'd still probably grab a Galaxy if I fancied one, mind.

